{
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": false
  },
  "name": "Run an ElevenLabs voice assistant that manages Gmail, Google Calendar and Contacts with Claude",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "69c6fd7d-ba91-52bd-ad99-2487d8b8e418",
      "name": "Note: About this template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -760,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 600,
        "height": 1080,
        "content": "## Talk to your inbox and calendar through an ElevenLabs voice agent\n\nSay \"move my 3pm with Dana to Thursday\" or \"draft a reply to the last email from my accountant\" and it gets done. ElevenLabs handles the voice, and this workflow does the work with Claude and your Google account.\n\n### How it works\n1. Your **ElevenLabs agent** calls this webhook as a tool, sending the request and its conversation ID.\n2. An optional shared secret rejects other callers, and empty requests get a 400.\n3. One **Claude** agent with 11 tools searches and drafts email, manages calendar events and looks up or saves contacts. Memory is keyed to the ElevenLabs conversation, so follow-ups work.\n4. The answer is cleaned for speech and sent back for the agent to say.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect **Anthropic**, **Gmail**, **Google Calendar** and **Google Contacts** credentials.\n2. In **Settings**, set `calendar_id` to your Google account email (that is your main calendar's ID), plus `timezone`, `owner_name` and an optional `shared_secret`.\n3. Click **Execute workflow** to run the pinned sample, then activate.\n4. Add the Production URL to your ElevenLabs agent as a webhook tool (see the note on the right).\n\n### Customization tips\nSwap Haiku for Sonnet for harder requests, or remove the Send email tool to make the assistant draft-only.\n\n_Built by Alicia Graham, economist and n8n Ambassador._"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8a487668-3b7c-5662-8405-80e424c178b7",
      "name": "Note: Receive and check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -120,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1360,
        "height": 780,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and check\nReads the request and conversation ID, checks the optional `x-api-key` secret (401) and rejects empty requests (400)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "870ecab3-a363-5126-bf6a-718a592608c7",
      "name": "Note: Assistant",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1280,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1240,
        "height": 1160,
        "content": "## 2. The assistant\nOne Claude agent and 11 Google tools. Memory keeps the last 20 turns of each ElevenLabs conversation."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2bce5266-061e-5ee8-8c86-6e54ec9ee2f4",
      "name": "Note: Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2560,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 780,
        "content": "## 3. Reply for speech\nRemoves markdown and line breaks so the voice reads it naturally."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "71c468a0-ea0d-5c21-b900-a4465b5fa1c8",
      "name": "Note: ElevenLabs tool",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3120,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### ElevenLabs tool setup\nAdd a **Webhook** tool to your agent: POST to the Production URL with body fields `query` (the user's full request) and `conversation_id` (dynamic variable `system__conversation_id`), plus an `x-api-key` header if you set a secret. Allow a 30-second timeout."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "246f78a5-1c10-547c-852e-24b01df42260",
      "name": "Warning: Real actions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3120,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "### This assistant acts on your real accounts\nIt is told to read back and get a yes before sending email or deleting events. Test with drafts first, and remove **Send email** if you only want drafts."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
